          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            This page shows the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cayley+graph"} Cayley graph
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            elements,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sym
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym(3)
            and makes explicit some of its properties.
          %p
            In all of the following we abbreviate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutations"} permutations
            of 3 elements as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mi j
                  %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mn 3
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %mi k
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  i j k
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\left(
                  \\array{
                  1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3
                  \\\
                  i &amp; j &amp; k
                  }
                  \\right)
                  \\,.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The following shows the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cayley+graph"} Cayley graph
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+groups"} symmetric groups
            on 3 elements,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
